- Fortune Teller 1/3 can block the 3/3 Swamp — Fortune Teller dies, Swamp takes 1 damage (survives as 3/3 with 1 damage). Hmm, actually 1 damage to a 3/3 doesn't kill it.\n\
- Fortune Teller blocks Long Feng 3/4 — Fortune Teller dies, Long Feng survives.\n\
- Corrupt Court Official 1/1 blocks anything and dies.\n\
\n\
Incoming damage if no blocks: 3 + 3 = 6 damage, taking me from 20 to 14.\n\
\n\
Wait, interesting note: Deadly Precision was cancelled twice before due to engine payment issues. I have Deadly Precision in hand. I have 2 untapped lands — wait, which lands are untapped? Island (tapped), Swamp (tapped), and untapped: Boiling Rock Prison and Swamp. So I have {B} and {B/R} available = 2 black mana potentially.\n\
\n\
I could cast Deadly Precision during combat! But wait — the additional cost is pay {4} or sacrifice an artifact or creature. I only have 2 mana untapped, so I can't pay {4}. But I can sacrifice an artifact or creature. I have a Clue token!\n\
\n\
So during declare blockers, I could:\n\
1. Block with Fortune Teller on Long Feng, then sacrifice... no wait.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think about the best play here.\n\
\n\
Option A: Cast Deadly Precision sacrificing the Clue token to kill Long Feng before blockers... but wait, it's declare blockers step. If I cast Deadly Precision now, it goes on the stack, and I can kill one of the attackers before damage. But I need to be careful — the choice to cast happens now during declare blockers.\n\
\n\
Actually, the prompt says \"Select blockers\" with choices including Clue Token [activate], Fortune Teller, Corrupt Court Official. I can declare blockers and also potentially cast spells. Let me think.\n\
\n\
Best play: Block the 3/3 Swamp with Fortune Teller (1/3) — Fortune Teller dies but the Swamp survives. Hmm, that's bad. Actually wait — blocking the 3/3 with a 1/3 means Fortune Teller dies and Swamp takes 1. Not great.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, block Long Feng with Fortune Teller (1/3 vs 3/4) — Fortune Teller dies, Long Feng survives.\n\
\n\
