\n\
Opponent (PilotB): 20hp, 1 card in hand. Battlefield: Food Token, Forest x2 (tapped), Leaves from the Vine (lore=2), Long Feng 3/4 (tapped, attacking), Pirate Peddlers 2/2 (sick), Swamp 3/3 (tapped, attacking), Swamp (tapped). All lands tapped. Graveyard includes Rockalanche with flashback {5}{G}.\n\
\n\
My plan from last turn: play The Fire Nation Drill, tap it on ETB to destroy Long Feng (power 4 or less — Long Feng is 3/4, power 3, so it qualifies). Then crew it with Teller + Official (power 1+1=2) — wait, when a Vehicle enters and I tap it for its ETB trigger, can I still crew it? Tapping the Vehicle doesn't prevent crewing. Crew cost is tap creatures with total power 2 or more. The Vehicle being tapped doesn't matter for attacking? Actually, a tapped creature can't attack. If I tap the Drill for its ETB trigger, then crew it, it becomes a creature but it's tapped, so it can't attack this turn. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Wait, let me re-read: \"When this enters, you may tap it. When you do, destroy target creature with power 4 or less.\" So I tap it as part of the ETB trigger to destroy Long Feng. Then it's tapped. Crewing it makes it a creature but it stays tapped, so it can't attack this turn. That's fine — the main goal is killing Long Feng.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, I could not tap it on ETB, crew it, and attack for 4 trample. But killing Long Feng is more important — Long Feng is their value engine that grows creatures whenever lands/creatures die.\n\
