\n\
Actually wait, the Drill is a Vehicle, not a creature. Its ETB trigger destroys Long Feng. Then opponent still has: Pirate Peddlers 2/2 deathtouch, Swamp 3/3 earthbent, Food token, Leaves from the Vine (lore=2, will go to lore=3 next turn and they draw a card), and lands.\n\
\n\
Option B: Deadly Precision on Long Feng ({B} + sacrifice Clue). Then I have 3 lands left for... Messenger Hawk ({2}{U/B}) — yes, I could cast both Deadly Precision and Messenger Hawk. That kills Long Feng and develops a flier with a Clue.\n\
\n\
Option C: Lost Days on Long Feng ({4}{U}) — puts it second from top or bottom, creates a Clue. Uses all 4 mana. Leaves them with the 3/3 Swamp and Peddlers.\n\
\n\
Hmm. Which is best? The Drill gives me a lasting 4/4 trample vehicle that can also kill future creatures... no wait, the destroy is only on ETB. After that it's just a 4/4 trample crew 2 vehicle.\n\
\n\
The Drill plan: kill Long Feng, leave Island untapped (nothing to do with it, or hold up... nothing). Board after: Drill (tapped artifact), Teller 1/3, Official 1/1, Clue token. \n\
\n\
The Deadly Precision + Messenger Hawk plan: kill Long Feng, get a 1/2 flier + Clue token. Board: Teller, Official, Hawk 1/2 flying, Clue x2. More board presence, more cards via Clues.\n\
\n\
Actually, the Deadly Precision sacrifice cost: \"pay {4} or sacrifice an artifact or creature\". I sacrifice the Clue token. So Deadly Precision costs {B} + Clue. Then Messenger Hawk {2}{U/B} using Island + Swamp + Swamp. Total mana: {B} + {2}{U/B} = works with 4 lands (Prison=B for DP, Island=U, Swamp, Swamp for Hawk). Yes!\n\
\n\
That gives me: Long Feng dead, board of Teller 1/3, Official 1/1, Hawk 1/2 flying, 2 Clues (the one I have plus the new one from Hawk... wait no, I sacrifice my existing Clue for DP, then Hawk ETB makes a new Clue. So net 1 Clue).\n\
\n\
Hmm wait, actually should I crack the Clue instead of sacrificing? No — sacrificing to DP is the cost, it replaces paying {4}.\n\
\n\
Compare with Drill plan: Drill kills Long Feng and leaves me a 4/4 trampler I can crew next turn. But this turn it taps itself for the kill, so no attack. And I use all my mana (well, Island left over).\n\
\n\
Actually, can I do Drill AND something else? Drill = {2}{B}{B} (4 mana). I have exactly 4 lands. So no.\n\
\n\
Deadly Precision + Hawk = kills Long Feng + develops board + Clue. Drill = kills Long Feng + big body for next turns.\n\
\n\
Opponent's board after Long Feng dies either way: 3/3 earthbent Swamp, 2/2 deathtouch Peddlers, Food, Leaves (lore 2→3, they draw a card next turn, then saga sacrifices). \n\
\n\
The threat: Rockalanche in graveyard with flashback {5}{G}. They have 2 Forests + 2 Swamps + ... they have Forest, Forest, Swamp (3/3 creature land), Swamp. Next turn they untap 4 lands. Flashback Rockalanche costs {5}{G} — they can't cast it next turn (only 4 lands, and only 2 green). But later it's a threat: earthbend X where X = Forests = 2, so a 2/2 land.\n\
\n\
Also Leaves from the Vine chapter III: draw a card if there's a creature or Lesson card in graveyard — Long Feng will be in graveyard, so they draw.\n\
\n\
I think the Deadly Precision + Messenger Hawk play is better for board development. But wait — can the Drill attack next turn? Crew 2 means tap creatures with total power 2+. Teller (1) + Official (1) = 2. So yes, next turn I can crew and attack with a 4/4 trample. That's strong pressure.\n\
\n\
Actually, hold on. Let me reconsider: should I kill Long Feng at all, or kill the 3/3 Swamp? Long Feng is 3/4 and grows things when stuff dies. The 3/3 Swamp when it dies returns to battlefield tapped (earthbend). Killing the Swamp just gives them back a tapped land — bad trade for my removal. Long Feng is the better target: it's their engine and a 3/4 body.\n\
\n\
Decision: Deadly Precision (sac Clue) on Long Feng + Messenger Hawk. Or Drill?\n\
\n\
Let me think about longer-term. My hand after DP+Hawk: Lost Days, Pirate Peddlers, The Fire Nation Drill. Next turn I draw a card, have 5 lands (if I draw a land... I have 28 cards in library). I could play Drill next turn with 5 mana... Drill is 4 mana, so I'd have 1 left over.\n\
\n\
With the Drill plan now: hand after = Deadly Precision, Lost Days, Messenger Hawk, Pirate Peddlers. Next turn: 5 mana (4 lands + maybe drawn land). Could cast Drill... already cast. Could cast Messenger Hawk + Deadly Precision (B + 2U/B = 4 mana) to kill the 3/3 Swamp... which returns tapped. Meh. Or Lost Days the Swamp ({4}{U}) — puts it on bottom, they lose the counters, get a Clue for me. That's actually decent vs the earthbent land: it goes into their library, and when... wait, earthbend says \"When it dies or is exiled, return it to the battlefield tapped.\" Lost Days puts it into the library — not dies or exiled, so it just goes away. They lose a land but the earthbend recursion is avoided. Hmm, but they get to redraw it eventually (bottom of library, so late).\n\
\n\
Hmm, both plans are reasonable. Let me weigh:\n\
\n\
Drill plan turn 5: Kill Long Feng. Board: Drill (tapped), Teller, Official, Clue. Mana left: Island (can't use). \n\
Turn 6: crew Drill (Teller+Official), attack for 4 trample into... their board: 3/3 Swamp, 2/2 deathtouch Peddlers. They block with Peddlers (deathtouch kills Drill? Drill is a creature when crewed — deathtouch destroys it). Trample: 4/4 vs 2/2 deathtouch — 2 damage tramples over... assign 2 to Peddlers (lethal), 2 to face. Drill dies to deathtouch. Hmm, that's bad. They'll just chump with deathtouch Peddlers.\n\
\n\
Alternatively they block with 3/3 Swamp: Drill 4/4 kills 3/3, Swamp returns tapped, Drill survives (takes 3). 1 trample damage. That's fine for me.\n\
\n\
DP+Hawk plan turn 5: Kill Long Feng. Board: Teller, Official, Hawk 1/2, Clue. \n\
Turn 6: draw, maybe play Drill and kill... Drill ETB can kill the 3/3 Swamp or Peddlers (power ≤4, both qualify). Kill Peddlers (deathtouch threat) — then attack with Hawk for 1.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually with DP+Hawk plan, next turn I play Drill and kill their Pirate Peddlers (the deathtoucher), then my board is much better.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually — why not this turn: Drill, tap ETB, kill Long Feng. Then next turn DP the Peddlers (sac Clue). Hmm.\n\
\n\
Let me think about what matters: opponent at 20, me at 14. Their pressure: 3/3 Swamp + Peddlers + whatever they draw. Leaves gives them a card next turn. They have 1 card in hand.\n\
