Actually wait — there's a subtlety. Should I use Deadly Precision on Long Feng now, or save it and use Drill's ETB to kill Long Feng, saving DP for later? If I use Drill now: Drill taps itself (can't attack this turn anyway due to... well, crewed vehicles can attack the turn they enter if crewed by non-sick creatures — but my creatures aren't sick). Actually Drill enters, I choose to tap it for ETB kill. It stays tapped. Can't attack. Then next turn it's a 4/4 I can crew.\n\
\n\
If I use DP now + Hawk, then Drill next turn kills another creature (Peddlers) AND can be crewed to attack? No wait — if Drill taps itself for the ETB kill, it can't attack that turn. Crew requires the vehicle to... crewing a tapped vehicle is fine, it becomes a tapped creature, can't attack. So Drill's ETB kill always costs it a turn of attacking. Unless I don't use the ETB kill and just crew+attack.\n\
\n\
OK here's my line: DP on Long Feng (sac Clue) + Messenger Hawk now. Next turn: Drill ETB kill Peddlers, or crew and attack depending on board.\n\
\n\
Actually, one more consideration: opponent's Pirate Peddlers — \"Whenever you sacrifice another permanent, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\" They have a Food token. If they sac Food, Peddlers becomes 3/3 and they gain 3. Also Long Feng triggers when a creature/land goes to graveyard — Food is an artifact, not creature/land, so no Long Feng trigger from Food. Fine.\n\
\n\
Also, when Long Feng dies to my DP — it's their creature, goes to their graveyard. Leaves chapter III will draw them a card (creature in graveyard). Unavoidable.\n\
\n\
Alright, let me also double check Deadly Precision targeting: \"Destroy target creature.\" Long Feng is a 3/4. No hexproof/indestructible mentioned. Opponent is tapped out (all lands tapped), 1 card in hand — could be a trick but they have no mana. Safe.\n\
\n\
