One more thought: should I hold DP and instead Lost Days Long Feng? Lost Days {4}{U}: owner puts it second from top or bottom, I create a Clue. That uses all 4 mana, leaves Long Feng out of their graveyard (no Leaves draw... actually they'd put it on bottom probably, or second from top to redraw it — they'd choose bottom... no wait, the OWNER chooses. They'd put it second from top to redraw Long Feng quickly? Or bottom to... they'd definitely put it second from top if they want it back, but it costs them a draw step and recast mana. Hmm, actually putting second from top means they draw it next turn. That's bad for me — they recast Long Feng. They'd choose second from top. So Lost Days on Long Feng = they get it back next turn + I get a Clue. Bad. Unless... they'd choose bottom? Why would they? Long Feng is their engine. They'd take it back. So Lost Days is weak here. Better used on the earthbent Swamp (they lose counters and the land goes away — they'd put it second from top? It's just a Swamp, they might put it bottom. Either way the 3/3 threat is gone and doesn't come back via earthbend since it didn't die).\n\
