\n\
So I have no mana left this turn. Postcombat I can't cast anything (Pirate Peddlers costs {2}{B}, Fire Nation Drill {2}{B}{B}, Lost Days {4}{U}).\n\
\n\
So: skip attack, pass to end turn.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — should I attack at all? Let me double-check. Attacking with both: opponent blocks Teller with Peddlers (deathtouch), Teller dies, Official deals 1. Opponent goes to 19, I lose Teller. Not worth it.\n\
\n\
Attack with Official only: blocked by Peddlers, Official dies. Not worth.\n\
\n\
Skip. Then next turn (turn 6), I'll have 5 mana (if I draw a land) — I can cast The Fire Nation Drill {2}{B}{B}, ETB tap to destroy a creature with power 4 or less — that kills Pirate Peddlers or the 3/3 Swamp. Then crew with Teller + Official (power 2) and attack with a 4/4 trample... wait, what's the Drill's stats? The Fire Nation Drill {2}{B}{B}: Trample, ETB destroy creature power 4 or less, Crew 2. Stats not shown — probably 4/4 or similar. Actually the text doesn't show power/toughness. Hmm, it's a Vehicle. Let me check oracle text later. Probably fine.\n\
\n\
Alternatively Lost Days on the 3/3 Swamp... that costs {4}{U}, puts it second from top or bottom. The earthbent Swamp when it leaves... actually earthbend returns it when it dies or is exiled — but Lost Days puts it into the library, not dies/exiled, so it wouldn't return! That's a nice answer to the 3/3.\n\
\n\
