\n\
Hmm wait, actually — should I attack with BOTH Teller and Hawk to pressure? No — Ruffians blocks Teller, trade, I lose crew capability and they get a 2/2 haste. No.\n\
\n\
So: cast Drill, kill Peddlers, pass (no attack). Keep 1 Swamp untapped (B) — irrelevant, nothing to cast with 1 mana. Fine.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait — should I consider NOT using the ETB tap-and-destroy, keeping the Drill untapped to... no, destroying a creature is the whole point. The Drill enters tapped when using ETB — that's fine, it wasn't going to attack this turn anyway (it has haste? No, Vehicles don't have haste; even crewed, it'd be summoning sick this turn! A Vehicle that enters this turn, when crewed, becomes a creature — does it have summoning sickness? Yes! It became a creature this turn... actually summoning sickness depends on when the permanent entered, not when it became a creature. The Drill entered this turn → if it becomes a creature, it's summoning sick → can't attack. So the Drill can't attack this turn regardless. ETB tap is free.)\n\
\n\
So the plan is solid. Let me also double check the ETB target legality: \"destroy target creature with power 4 or less.\" Peddlers is 3/3 (power 3). Legal. Ruffians 3/1 (power 3). Legal. Swamp 3/3 (power 3). Legal. I'll choose Peddlers (p49).\n\
