      "reasoning": "Combat resolved — the Ruffians and my Fortune Teller traded, their second Swamp got earthbent into a 2/2, and I took 3 (11→8). They just cast a Boiling Rock Rioter postcombat. Let me check what it does.",
      "thinking": "Combat resolved: I took 3 from the 3/3 Swamp (11→8, matches), Fortune Teller killed the Ruffians and... wait, Fortune Teller is in my graveyard. So the Ruffians dealt 3 to Fortune Teller (3 power ≥ 3 toughness) — Fortune Teller died too. And Fortune Teller's 1 damage didn't matter since Ruffians has toughness 1 — yes, 1 damage kills the 3/1. So both died. Ruffians' death trigger earthbent 2 onto their other Swamp (p37), making it a 2/2.\n\
\n\
Hmm, so I lost Fortune Teller. That changes my crew plan! Now my creatures: Messenger Hawk (1/2, power 1... but wait, it's \"modified\" — it gets +2/+0 if I've drawn 2+ cards this turn; currently 1/2). To crew the Drill (Crew 2), I need total power 2 among tapped creatures. Messenger Hawk alone is power 1 — not enough!\n\
\n\
So I need another creature. My hand: Pirate Peddlers (2/2, {2}{B}). Hawk (1) + Peddlers (2) = 3 power ≥ 2. That works.\n\
\n\
Also I could draw cards to pump Hawk: if I draw 2+ cards in a turn, Hawk becomes 3/2 and can crew alone. E.g., crack the Clue + Boiling Rock Prison sacrifice... that draws 2 cards → Hawk becomes 3/2, can crew alone, and hits as a 3/2 flyer. Interesting line.\n\
\n\
Now opponent just cast something postcombat: \"Boiling Rock Rioter\" is on the stack. They have 1 card in hand, tapped 2 Forests... wait, board shows Forest (tapped), Forest (tapped), Forest, and the stack has Boiling Rock Rioter. What does it do? Let me get oracle text. It's probably a creature with some ETB. Let me check.\n\
\n\
Actually let me get oracle text for Boiling Rock Rioter to understand thethreat.",
