\n\
Actually wait — should I have cracked the Clue precombat to make Hawk 3/2? Cards drawn this turn: 1 (my draw step). If I sacrifice Clue to draw, that's 2 cards drawn, Hawk becomes 3/2, attack for 3 instead of 1. That's a real consideration but the decision point is already at declare attackers. The pass_priority skipped to declare_attackers. I can't go back. So just attack with Hawk for 1.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually could I still crack the clue before damage? Cracking clue in combat after attackers declared — the +2/+0 applies \"as long as you've drawn two or more cards this turn\" — it's a static ability, so if I draw a second card during combat (after blocks), Hawk becomes 3/2 before combat damage. Yes! Static abilities update continuously. So: declare Hawk as attacker, then in declare blockers / after blockers, sacrifice Clue token to draw a card → Hawk becomes 3/2 → deals 3 instead of 2... wait it deals 1 base, +2 = 3 power. So 3 damage instead of 1.\n\
\n\
Wait, base 1/2, +2/+0 = 3/2. Deals 3 damage. That's 2 extra damage for cracking the clue. Worth it? The Clue is worth a card; 2 extra damage is nice but the card might be better. Hmm. Actually cracking the clue draws me a card anyway — I'm trading the clue for a fresh card plus 2 extra damage. That seems good. The clue otherwise sits there; I have 26 cards in library, drawing is fine.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think: is there any risk? They have one untapped Forest and 1 card in hand. Could they have a trick? If they had a removal for the Hawk... The Hawk is attacking unblocked regardless (no flyers/reach on their board). So drawing a card to pump it is safe — worst case they kill the Hawk in response to the clue activation, but they'd kill it anyway if they could. Actually if they kill the Hawk, I still drew the card. Fine.\n\
\n\
So plan: attack with Messenger Hawk. Then when I get priority again (declare blockers step or after), sacrifice the Clue to draw, pumping Hawk to 3/2, dealing 3.\n\
\n\
Wait, but mana: Clue costs {2} to sacrifice. I have 2 untapped Swamps. That works ({B}{B} can pay generic {2}).\n\
\n\
Alternatively, save the clue for later? The 2 extra damage now vs. having a card later. I'm at 8 life, they're at 19. I need to close the game. My board: Drill (can crew with Hawk + Peddlers next turn), Peddlers, Hawk. Their board will untap: Rioter 3/3, two earthbent Swamps 3/3 and 2/2. They're going to swing big next turn. I'm at 8. I need to race. Extra damage matters. Also the Clue draws me toward action — I have only Lost Days and Swampsnare Trap in hand, both situational.\n\
\n\
Actually, one concern: racing math. They're at 19. My damage output per turn: Hawk 1 (or 3), Drill 4 (crew), Peddlers 2... They have blockers though. Rioter + 2 earthbent lands can block. Drill has trample. Hmm.\n\
