Alternative: don't crew; block 3/3 with Peddlers (deathtouch trade, pump-proof), take 2 from the 2/2 → 6 life. Result: Peddlers dies, 3/3 Swamp returns tapped. My board: Drill, Hawk, 5 lands. Their board: Rioter, 2/2 Swamp, 3/3 Swamp (tapped), Food, 2 cards.\n\
\n\
vs. crew line (assuming Drill 4/4): Drill blocks 3/3, both deal damage, Swamp dies returns tapped, Drill survives as 4/1 effectively (damage cleans up at EOT — Drill takes 3, toughness 4, survives; damage removed at cleanup). I take 2 → 6. Board: Drill, Peddlers (tapped), Hawk. Same life, but I keep Peddlers AND Drill. Strictly better — UNLESS they have a pump trick (then Drill dies and 3/3 lives: catastrophe) or a kill spell for the Drill... same risk any turn.\n\
\n\
Do they have a trick? 2 cards in hand, 3 Forests untapped. Avatar green tricks... \"Earthbending\" themed. Possible. But Peddlers line loses my Peddlers for certain. The crew line's downside requires a specific trick. Also — if they had a trick, would they attack both Swamps into my board knowing I could crew? They might be betting on the trick. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Middle path: crew Drill, block the 2/2 with Drill (kills it, Drill takes 2 — survives at any toughness ≥3; only dies to a +1-or-more pump... if they pump the 2/2 to kill Drill, Drill's 4 damage vs pumped toughness ~4-5 might not kill it — bad). Ugh, tricks complicate everything.\n\
\n\
Let me think about what tricks exist in this format (Avatar TLA). Green instant pump... I recall \"Bumi's...\"? Not sure. There's likely a generic +1/+1 or +2/+2 earthbend trick. Honestly, in limited, attacking both lands into an open crew-the-Drill board suggests either a trick or just pressure. \n\
\n\
Also consider: they have 3 Forests untapped but only 2 cards. Rockalanche flashback needs {5}{G} — they have exactly 3 Forests + 2 Swamp-lands (tapped/attacking). Not enough for flashback. So no instant-speed Rockalanche. \n\
\n\
What about a trick making the 3/3 survive AND kill Drill? E.g., +2/+2: 5/5 vs Drill 4/4: Drill deals 4 (not lethal to 5 toughness), takes 5 (lethal). Drill dies, Swamp lives, I took 2 from the other Swamp → 6, and lost Drill + (Peddlers survives but tapped). Terrible.\n\
\n\
How likely is a trick? In limited, decent chance in 2 cards with 3 green open... but also they telegraphed \"let's see if the earthbent lands can keep the pressure on\" — sounds like just pressing, and if they had a trick they might've held back one land? Eh.\n\
\n\
Alternative safer line: block 3/3 with Peddlers (no crew). Guaranteed trade (deathtouch), take 2 → 6. Keep Drill + Hawk. Next turn: Swampsnare Trap Rioter ({2}{B}), crew Drill with Hawk (power 1 < 2 — NOT enough alone!). Uh oh: crew 2 needs total power ≥ 2. Hawk is 1 power (or 3 if I drew 2 cards). Hawk alone can't crew unless pumped to 3 (drawn 2+ cards). I'd need to cast something: Foggy Swamp Hunters {3}{B} (3 power) — with 5 lands: Swampsnare ({2}{B}) + Hunters ({3}{B}) = {5}{B}{B}... mana: 5 lands = 5 mana, costs 3+3=6 total. Can't do both. \n\
\n\
Turn 8 with 5 mana: cast Hunters ({3}{B}) → crew Drill with Hunters + Hawk (3+1) → attack Drill + Hawk + Hunters? Hunters sick, tapped crewing. Attack Drill (4/4 trample) + Hawk (1/2 or 3/2). Blockers: Rioter 3/3, 2/2 Swamp (3/3 Swamp returns tapped). They double-block Drill → Drill dies (4 toughness vs 5 power)... or block Hawk? no flyers. Hmm, Drill double-blocked: 4 damage split 3/1, Drill takes 5, dies. Not great. Alternatively Swampsnare the Rioter ({2}{B}), then crew needs 2 power: Hawk (1) + ...nothing else (Peddlers dead in this line). Can't crew! Drill is useless turn 8 without a crew. So the no-crew line strands the Drill on turn 8 unless I cast Hunters and crew with it, but then I can't kill Rioter and Drill gets double-blocked and dies.\n\
\n\
Whereas the crew-now line keeps Peddlers alive: turn 8, Swampsnare Rioter ({2}{B}), crew Drill with Peddlers (3≥2), attack Drill + Hawk. Blockers: only 2/2 Swamp (3/3 returns tapped, Rioter dead). Drill tramples: 2 to Swamp, 2-3 through. Good.\n\
\n\
So crewing now (keeping Peddlers) is much better for my turn 8, provided no pump trick. I'll take the risk — it's the higher-EV line. Also, flavor: the Drill holds the line!\n\
\n\
Actually — one more subtle option: crew the Drill AND block with Drill, but choose which attacker after seeing stats. If Drill is 4/4: block 3/3 (best). If Drill is 5/4: block 3/3. If 4/3: block 2/2 (kill it, survive with 1 damage left... 4/3 takes 2 → survives; deals 4 to 2/2, kills). Let me go: activate crew on p9, select Peddlers p52 as crew.\n\
\n\
