Wait, could I instead block p22 (3/3) and take 2 (8→6)? Peddlers (3/3) blocks 3/3: Peddlers takes 3 → dies. No, deathtouch kills p22 but Peddlers dies too. p22 returns tapped as a land with no counters... wait, does it? The earthbent land: \"When it dies or is exiled, return it to the battlefield tapped.\" So it returns tapped as a plain Swamp land (no longer a creature, no counters). So blocking p22 trades my Peddlers for removing their 3/3 attacker (it becomes a tapped land). Then I take 2 from p37 (8→6).\n\
\n\
Hmm, which is better? Option A: block p37, Peddlers survives, take 3 (→5), p37 becomes tapped land, p22 (3/3) remains as attacker. Option B: block p22, Peddlers dies, take 2 (→6), p22 becomes tapped land, p37 (2/2) remains.\n\
\n\
Option A keeps Peddlers alive, which is my deathtouch wall + crew piece. I go to 5. Opponent still has a 3/3 attacker (p22). Next turn (my turn 9), I untap Hawk, crew Drill with Hawk + Peddlers, and can attack or keep back.\n\
\n\
Their board after option A: p22 3/3 earthbent Swamp (untaps next turn), Swamp land (tapped, was p37), Rioter 3/3, Food, 3 Forests. They have 2 cards in hand. I'm at 5. If they attack with p22 (3/3) + Rioter (3/3) next turn, that's 6 damage — I must block or die. My blockers: Peddlers (3/3 deathtouch), Hawk (1/2 flyer), Drill (can crew). With Peddlers + crewed Drill I can block both and kill both (Drill trample... as blocker, Drill with its P/T — if it's a 5/4, it kills Rioter and survives 3 damage; Peddlers kills p22 and survives 2 damage... wait p22 is 3/3, Peddlers 3/3 blocks: takes 3 → dies. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — with 5 life facing 6 power of attackers, I need to block at least 1. Blocking p22 with Peddlers (both die-ish, Peddlers dies), blocking Rioter with Drill (Drill presumably 5/4 kills it, survives). Then take 0. That works but loses Peddlers.\n\
\n\
Option B: I go to 6, Peddlers dead. Their attackers: p37 2/2 + Rioter 3/3 = 5 power. I can block Rioter with crewed Drill and take 2 (→4), or block both (Hawk chumps 2/2, Drill eats Rioter).\n\
\n\
Hmm, both lines are defensible. Option A keeps my best creature. Also in option A, the 2/2 dies to deathtouch and becomes a tapped land — but importantly it stays a land permanently? \"return it to the battlefield tapped\" — it returns as a land (the land card), no longer a creature since the earthbend effect ended when it left the battlefield. Yes, it's just a tapped Swamp now. So their creature count drops.\n\
\n\
In option A, I keep Peddlers alive and can also crew the Drill on my turn 9 and swing: Drill (5/4 trample?) + Peddlers... actually I could attack with Drill crewed by Hawk+Peddlers, and Peddlers can also attack (3/3 deathtouch, sick until my turn 9 — it was cast turn 7, so on turn 9 it's fine). Hawk 1/2 flyer. That's a big swing: Drill 5 trample + Peddlers 3 + Hawk... they have Rioter 3/3 and p22 3/3 to block. Drill tramples over.\n\
\n\
But wait — attacking taps my blockers, and I'm at 5 facing lethal-ish. Risky. Better to crew Drill and stay back on defense? Crew lasts until end of turn — if I crew on my turn and don't attack, Drill stops being a creature at end of turn and can't block on their turn unless I crew again (crew is only on my turn... crew can be activated any time I have priority at sorcery... no, crew can be activated at instant speed! Crew is an activated ability with no timing restriction). So on their turn, I can crew the Drill when they attack to block.\n\
\n\
OK so keeping Peddlers alive (Option A) is my summary's stated plan. Let me stick with it: block p37 with Peddlers, take 3, go to 5.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me reconsider life math. Option A: I'm at 5. Their board for next attack: p22 3/3, Rioter 3/3, plus whatever they cast (2 cards in hand, 5+ lands untapped... they have 3 Forests + Boiling Rock Rioter + lands: Forest x3, Swamp p22 creature-land, and the returned Swamp land p37 tapped). Mana: 3 Forests + p22 (Swamp, can tap for B) = 4 mana + firebending. They could cast something. With 2 unknown cards.\n\
\n\
If they attack with p22 + Rioter (6 power) into my 5 life: I crew Drill (tap Hawk + Peddlers... wait, crew taps creatures with total power 2+; Hawk has power 1 + Peddlers power 3 = 4 ≥ 2). But if I tap Peddlers to crew, Peddlers can't block. Then Drill blocks one (kills it, takes 3), and... I'd take 3 from the other → 2 life. Or Drill blocks Rioter (3/3): Drill 5/4 kills Rioter, takes 3 (toughness 4, survives). p22 gets through for 3 → I'm at 2. Then next turn... they still have p22.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, don't crew; block p22 with Peddlers (Peddlers dies, kills p22), take 3 from Rioter → 2 life. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Or block Rioter with Peddlers (deathtouch kills Rioter, Peddlers survives 3 damage? Peddlers is 3/3, takes 3 → dies. Ugh, 3 toughness vs 3 power = dead).\n\
\n\
Hmm wait, Peddlers is 3/3 with the +1/+1 counter. Blocking a 3/3: takes 3 damage, 3 toughness → dies. Yes.\n\
\n\
So any block by Peddlers on a 3-power creature kills Peddlers. Blocking the 2/2 p37: takes 2, survives with 2 damage marked. That's why blocking p37 now is right — Peddlers survives this combat.\n\
\n\
But note: damage marked stays until cleanup. Peddlers will have 2 damage marked until end of turn — it heals at cleanup (their turn's cleanup). So on my turn 9 it's back to full 3 toughness. Good.\n\
\n\
Let me also consider: is there any chance they have a trick? They have 2 cards in hand and 3 untapped Forests + Rioter untapped (firebending 1 if it attacks — but it's not attacking). Actually during combat they could have a pump spell. If they pump p37 (my blocked 2/2) to kill Peddlers... e.g., a +2/+2 pump makes it 4/4, Peddlers takes 4 → dies, and deathtouch still kills it. Then I take 3 from p22 → 5. Same life, but Peddlers dead. Risk exists but I can't play around everything; the alternative (blocking p22) loses Peddlers for sure. Taking the block on p37 is right.\n\
\n\
Also consider not blocking at all: take 5 → 3 life. Way too dangerous. No.\n\
\n\
So: blockers=\"p52:p37\".\n\
\n\
