- Boiling Rock Rioter 3/3 (untapped)\n\
- Food Token\n\
- Forest x3\n\
- Swamp 2/2 earthbent (untapped)\n\
- Swamp (plain land)\n\
- 2 cards in hand\n\
\n\
Choices: attack with Messenger Hawk, Pirate Peddlers, all, or skip.\n\
\n\
My plan from the summary: attack with Messenger Hawk only (unblockable flyer — they have no flyers), keep Peddlers + Hunters back for defense.\n\
\n\
Wait, but should I consider attacking with Peddlers too? If I attack with Peddlers (3/3 deathtouch), they can block with Rioter 3/3 (trade — deathtouch kills Rioter, Peddlers dies to 3 damage) or the 2/2 Swamp (Peddlers kills it, takes 2, survives). They'd probably block with the 2/2 earthbent Swamp — the Swamp dies but returns tapped as a land... actually the earthbent Swamp when it dies returns to battlefield tapped as a land (with no counters? Actually it returns as a land, the earthbend effect says \"When it dies or is exiled, return it to the battlefield tapped\" — returns as a land, no longer a creature). So they lose the attacker but keep the land. They'd chump with the 2/2 Swamp and Peddlers survives with 2 damage marked. Then no damage gets through.\n\
\n\
But the real reason to keep Peddlers back: I'm at 3 life. Opponent has Rioter 3/3 and 2/2 Swamp. If they attack with both next turn, I need blockers. I have:\n\
- Pirate Peddlers 3/3 deathtouch\n\
- Foggy Swamp Hunters 3/4 (will be unsick next turn)\n\
- The Fire Nation Drill (can be crewed by tapping creatures with total power 2+)\n\
\n\
If I attack with Hawk only, I keep Peddlers, Hunters, and Drill (crewable) back. That's a strong defensive wall.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait — should I crew the Drill and attack with it? The Drill is 4/4 trample? Let me check its power/toughness. The Fire Nation Drill — Crew 2. Its P/T isn't shown in the rules text here. From earlier context: \"Drill plus Peddlers hits for exactly 8\" — so Drill is presumably 5/5? Actually \"Drill plus Peddlers hits for exactly 8\" — Peddlers is 3/3, so Drill would be 5 power. Hmm, or Drill is 4/4 and Peddlers 3... that's 7. Let me think. Earlier: \"my 3/3 deathtouch Peddlers is already the better attacker since Drill plus Peddlers hits for exactly 8.\" So Drill (5?) + Peddlers (3) = 8. So Drill is likely 5/4 or 5/5.\n\
\n\
Actually, I could look it up. The Fire Nation Drill is from the Avatar set. Let me recall... I don't remember exactly. Let me use get_oracle_text to check its P/T.\n\
\n\
But the key consideration: I'm at 3 life. If I tap out my creatures to attack, opponent swings back with Rioter + 2/2 Swamp for 5, and I have only Hunters (3/4) to block. Blocking the Rioter with Hunters: Hunters takes 3, survives (3/4), Rioter takes 3 and dies. Then 2/2 gets through for 2 → I go to 1. Hmm, that works actually. But they have 2 cards in hand — any burn spell or haste creature kills me. I'm at 3.\n\
\n\
Actually, defensive posture is right. Keep everything back, attack with Hawk only (free 1 damage, or 3 if I crack the Clue... but cracking the Clue costs {2} and I only have 1 untapped Swamp, so I can't crack it this turn).\n\
\n\
So: attack with Messenger Hawk only. It deals 1 (they're at 16 → 15). It's unblockable (no flyers on their side).\n\
\n\
Should I also attack with Peddlers? They'd block with the 2/2 Swamp (chump, returns tapped as land) — no damage, but it removes their 2/2 attacker permanently (returns as plain land). Hmm, that's actually a consideration: killing the 2/2 earthbent Swamp reduces their attacking force. But then Peddlers is tapped and can't block next turn... wait, no — if Peddlers attacks and survives, it's tapped, and on their turn it stays tapped (doesn't untap until my next untap step). So attacking with Peddlers leaves me with only Hunters + Drill (crewable by... what? Peddlers tapped, Hawk tapped, Hunters can't crew the turn it... actually Hunters is sick now but won't be next turn; on their turn, my untapped creatures would be Hunters only. Crew requires tapping creatures with total power 2+ — Hunters has 3 power, so Hunters alone could crew the Drill. But then Hunters is tapped and can't block, though the Drill becomes a 5/5 (or whatever) blocker.\n\
\n\
If I keep Peddlers back: on their turn I have Peddlers (3/3 deathtouch), Hunters (3/4), and Drill crewable by Peddlers+Hunters (power 3+3=6 ≥ 2). That's a lot of defense.\n\
\n\
Opponent's attackers next turn: Rioter 3/3, 2/2 Swamp. If they attack with both:\n\
- I block Rioter with Peddlers (deathtouch kills Rioter, Peddlers takes 3 and survives? Peddlers is 3/3, takes 3 → dies. Wait, 3 damage to a 3/3 kills it. So Peddlers trades with Rioter. Hmm, actually deathtouch means Peddlers kills Rioter, and Rioter's 3 damage kills Peddlers. Trade.\n\
- Or block Rioter with Hunters (3/4): Hunters survives, Rioter dies.\n\
- And block 2/2 with crewed Drill or just take 2.\n\
\n\
Anyway, defense is solid if I keep everything home. Attack with Hawk only.\n\
\n\
One more consideration: should I attack with the Drill itself? Crew it with Hawk + Peddlers and swing with Drill + Hawk? Drill is presumably 5/5 trample. They block with Rioter or 2/2... Drill tramples. If they block Drill with Rioter (3/3): Drill takes 3, survives (if 5 toughness), Rioter dies, trample 2 through. Hawk unblocked for 1. Total 3 damage, they lose Rioter. But then my board is all tapped: Hawk (tapped to crew), Peddlers (tapped to crew), Drill (attacking, tapped). Only Hunters untapped for their swing... they swing with 2/2 Swamp for 2 → I'm at 1. Plus 2 cards in hand could be anything (haste creature, burn). Too risky at 3 life.\n\
\n\
Conservative: attack with Hawk only. This matches my stated plan. Let me do that.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me double-check the Hawk's power. It's 1/2 base, gets +2/+0 if I've drawn 2+ cards this turn. I've drawn 1 card this turn (per the counter). I can't crack the Clue (only 1 untapped Swamp, need {2}). So Hawk is 1/2, hits for 1. Opp 16 → 15.\n\
\n\
Fine. Attack with Messenger Hawk only.",
