\n\
Decision: Line A (attack Hawk + Hunters) gains 3 life and deals 6 — putting them at 9 and me at 6, which actually gives MORE cushion than Line B in some scenarios? No wait — Line A leaves me with fewer blockers. Let me compare worst cases:\n\
\n\
Line A: me at 6, opp at 9. Their turn worst case (Rockalanche flashback, swing with 3): I have 1 blocker (Peddlers). Block Rioter, take 5 → at 1. My turn 11: opp at 9, board Rioter dead... wait Peddlers killed Rioter with deathtouch. Their board: Swamp 2/2, Land 3/3 (now just a land? No — earthbend creature stays a creature; the Rockalanche land is a 3/3 until it dies). Hmm wait, earthbend: \"Target land you control becomes a 0/0 creature with haste that's still a land. Put X +1/+1 counters on it.\" It stays a creature indefinitely (until it dies). So their board after: 2/2 Swamp, 3/3 land, Food. My turn 11: untap Hawk, Hunters, Peddlers. 6 lands. Attack: Drill (crew Peddlers) 5 trample + Hawk 1/2 (1 card drawn... after draw, 1 card; if I crack no clue — already used) + Hunters 3/4 (no lifelink/menace — only 1 card drawn) + Warden? They block with 2/2 + 3/3: Drill trample 5 — block with 3/3, take 2 trample... Let me not go too deep. Opp at 9, I have 5+4+1+3 = 13 power vs their 2 blockers (5 toughness). Likely lethal or near. Also I can cast Warden for the {3} ping reach.\n\
\n\
Line B: me at 3, opp at 12. Their turn worst case: take 2 → at 1. My turn 11: opp at 12, harder to kill.\n\
\n\
Line A seems better: gains life AND deals damage. The lifegain from Hunters (lifelink) offsets the risk. And killing them faster matters — they're at 9 vs 12, big difference with my board.\n\
\n\
But wait — Line A's risk: what if they DON'T flashback Rockalanche but instead hold up tricks with 2 cards? E.g., a burn spell to my face? I'm at 6 after lifegain vs at 3 in Line B. Line A's lifegain actually protects me MORE. The only downside of Line A is fewer blockers, but Peddlers 4/4 deathtouch is a great lone blocker.\n\
\n\
Hmm, one more consideration: in Line A, is Hunters really unblockable? Menace requires 2+ blockers. Their untapped creatures: only Rioter (Colony dies from the Trap, 2/2 Swamp is tapped). Yes — Hunters is unblockable. And Hawk flies (they have no flying/reach after Colony dies). So 6 damage guaranteed, +3 life.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually — is the Colony definitely dead? Board shows it as -1/1 still on battlefield with Swampsnare Trap attached. A creature with toughness ≤ 0 dies as a state-based action. The game will process it. By combat, it's dead. Yes.\n\
\n\
Also, should I crack the Clue BEFORE combat to enable all this? Yes — I need the 2nd card drawn for Hawk's +2/+0 and Hunters' lifelink/menace. Currently \"Cards you've drawn this turn: 1\". Crack Clue → 2 cards → bonuses active.\n\
\n\
