3. Combat: attack with Hawk + Hunters. Both unblockable. Deal 6 (15→9), gain 3 (3→6).\n\
4. Postcombat: 1 Swamp untapped, nothing to cast. Pass.\n\
\n\
Wait — after step 2, I have 1 untapped Swamp. Nothing costs {B} alone in my hand (Sold Out {3}{B}, Warden {2}{B/R}). Correct, nothing to cast.\n\
\n\
Actually, hold on — should I reconsider playing the Engine Room? Any downside? It enters tapped, so no mana loss this turn. Downside: none really, it's my land drop. Up next turn I have 6 lands. Play it.\n\
\n\
Hmm, one thing: is there any reason to keep the Clue instead of cracking? The Clue could be cracked on a later turn for the same effect. But the Peddlers counter + lifelink defense + extra 2 damage now is worth it. Also drawing a card now (22 lib) could hit something useful. Yes, crack it.\n\
\n\
Alternatively — cast Warden instead of cracking Clue, attack with Hawk (1) + Hunters? Hunters without lifelink/menace: blocked by Rioter (3/3 vs 3/4 — Hunters survives, Rioter... 3 damage to Rioter kills it! Hunters 3/4 blocked by Rioter 3/3: Hunters deals 3 to Rioter (dead), takes 3 (survives as 3/4 with 3 damage). That trades Rioter for nothing! Wait, that's actually good: if they block Hunters with Rioter, Rioter dies and Hunters survives. They might not block (then take 3). Hmm, but without menace they CAN single-block. So attacking Hunters without menace: they choose — block and lose Rioter (killing my Hunters? No: Hunters 3/4 takes 3 from Rioter, survives; Rioter takes 3, dies). They'd lose Rioter for nothing. So they don't block, take 3. Either way fine. But no lifegain.\n\
\n\
I prefer the Clue-crack line: lifegain + Peddlers growth + card draw.\n\
\n\
Let me also double check the Peddlers counter: \"Whenever you sacrifice another permanent, put a +1/+1 counter on {this}.\" Cracking the Clue = sacrificing an artifact (another permanent) → Peddlers gets a counter → 4/4. Yes.\n\
\n\
Alright, executing:\n\
1. Play Airship Engine Room.\n\
2. Crack Clue.\n\
3. Attack with Hawk + Hunters.\n\
\n\
