Actually, one thing: when Invasion Tactics resolves and its ETB goes on the stack, I get priority again. Still nothing. Then combat. Declare blockers — I have no untapped creatures, so no blocks. Then damage, I take 6, I die.\n\
\n\
Wait, unless the opponent attacks into... no. I'm dead unless they misplay.\n\
\n\
Let me reconsider — is my life really 6? \"life\":6 for PilotA. Yes. And I gained 3 from lifelink last turn (went to 6 per the log). Yes.\n\
\n\
Opponent life: 5.\n\
\n\
Damn, so close. If I survive one turn, I win (untap, crew Drill, swing for way more than 5). But I don't survive unless they misplay.\n\
\n\
Actually — wait. What if they DON'T attack with the Colony because they want to keep it back? No reason to — it's a 1/3, useless as a blocker against my ground creatures anyway (it has flying, could block my Hawk, but my Hawk is... it's my turn next, Hawk untaps). Hmm, actually a smart opponent might keep the Colony back to block my Messenger Hawk on my turn! If they keep Colony back, they only attack with Rioter for 5, I go to 1, survive, and then... my turn 11: I untap everything. They're at 5. I crew the Drill and swing with everything: Drill (5/5? let me check — Fire Nation Drill P/T... it's a Vehicle with trample; power probably 5 or so), Peddlers 4/4 deathtouch, Hunters 3/4 lifelink menace, Hawk 3/2 (if I draw 2). That's way more than 5. But they have blockers: Rioter 3/3 (tapped from attacking? no — it attacked, so it's tapped... actually after combat it stays tapped until their untap). On my turn, Rioter is tapped (attacked), Colony untapped (if held back). Colony blocks my Hawk (3/2 vs 1/3... Hawk 3/2 kills 1/3 Colony? 3 damage to 1/3 → 3 toughness, survives? No: 3 damage to toughness 3 = survives. And Colony deals 1 to Hawk's 2 toughness = survives. Hmm, or if Colony is 3/5 with counters, it blocks and kills Hawk? 3 power vs 2 toughness → Hawk dies.)\n\
\n\
Anyway — that's all moot if they just attack with both and kill me.\n\
\n\
Let me just pass priority and see what happens. There's literally no decision to make. I'll pass.\n\
\n\
Actually, hmm, let me reconsider whether I have any way to gain life or prevent damage. \n\
\n\
My board: Clue token? No — I cracked it last turn. Food token? No, that's theirs. \n\
\n\
Nothing. Pass.\n\
\n\
Let me also send a chat message — something like acknowledging the game might be over, or a \"gg\" or reacting to their Invasion Tactics play. Per instructions, I should chat at least once every 2 turn cycles. Let me send something.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me first pass priority and see the result, then chat based on what happens. Or chat now. Let me pass priority first.\n\
\n\
Let me write the summary for the pass. Actually pass_priority doesn't take a summary. Let me just call it.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually, I realize I should double-check: maybe I can still win this turn somehow if they attack. No — I have no blocks, no tricks. If they attack with both, I die.Let me pass and see.\n\
\n\
Let me call pass_priority.",
