      "chosen_args": {
        "summary": "My turn 8: I cast Lost Days (all 5 lands) and it's on the stack awaiting a target. I'm at 3 life; their board is Rioter 3/3, tapped 3/3 and 2/2 earthbent Swamps, Food, 5 lands, 2 cards in hand. Targeting the 3/3 earthbent Swamp — library removal doesn't trigger its earthbend return, permanently neutralizing their biggest attacker and cutting them to 4 lands (off Rockalanche flashback).",
        "choice": "p22",
        "rationale": "Targeting the 3/3 earthbent Swamp with Lost Days. Being put into the library is neither dying nor exile, so the earthbend return trigger never fires — it becomes a dead Swamp card in their deck. This removes the attacker that's lethal on its own against my 3 life and drops them to 4 lands on board, keeping them far from Rockalanche flashback mana.",
      },
