        "content": "{\"analysis\":\"Building a Blue-Black 'draw two cards a turn' / Clue synergy deck. Black is the deepest color by far, with a strong removal suite (2x Sold Out, Swampsnare Trap, Deadly Precision, Fatal Fissure, Azula Always Lies, plus The Fire Nation Drill) and cheap disruptive creatures (4x Corrupt Court Official, 3x Pirate Peddlers). Blue adds the payoff package: Wolfbat x2, Messenger Hawk, Foggy Swamp Hunters, and Otter-Penguin all reward drawing a second card, while Forecasting Fortune Teller, Messenger Hawk, Lost Days, and Clue-making removal fuel that plan. Clues also double as sacrifice fodder to grow the deathtouching Pirate Peddlers. Fatal Fissure combos with Deadly Precision for a kill plus earthbend 4. Vindictive Warden is playable off hybrid black mana as an extra menace threat (its {3} ping is colorless), so it takes the slot of the fourth, redundant Corrupt Court Official. Left in the sideboard: the entire red package (Zuko, Mai, Treetop Freedom Fighters, How to Start a Riot) since splashing off two tapped Boiling Rock Prisons would hurt the UB tempo; all white (Water Tribe Captain, Curious Farm Animals) and green (Kyoshi Island Plaza is blank with no Shrines, Earthbending Lesson); Cat-Gator and Geyser Leaper as too slow at the top end; Dai Li Indoctrination as redundant discard; and the fourth Corrupt Court Official. Lands: 17, roughly 9 Swamp / 7 Island plus the drafted Airship Engine Room as a blue source that can cash in for a card late.\", \"chosen_spells\":[\"Sold Out\",\"Sold Out\",\"Wolfbat\",\"Wolfbat\",\"Pirate Peddlers\",\"Pirate Peddlers\",\"Pirate Peddlers\",\"Corrupt Court Official\",\"Corrupt Court Official\",\"Corrupt Court Official\",\"Swampsnare Trap\",\"Foggy Swamp Hunters\",\"Vindictive Warden\",\"Hog-Monkey\",\"Azula Always Lies\",\"The Fire Nation Drill\",\"Messenger Hawk\",\"Fatal Fissure\",\"Deadly Precision\",\"Forecasting Fortune Teller\",\"Otter-Penguin\",\"Lost Days\",\"It'll Quench Ya!\"],\"decision\":\"accept\"}",
